From 335b88012dcb800b534824934b98356db750e0ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Meadlock <jmeadlock@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:19:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 824/826] fix(dsv41): keep DSML closers inside tool arguments
 unless structure follows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-60's series applied through 0816.

Rationale: DSML has no escaping. Candidate-60's token-provenance rule (0643,
#948/#949) keeps a quoted closer spelled in ordinary pieces as text, but when
the model emits the quoted closer as the genuine DSML token (as reported on
#876), a string argument that contains </｜DSML｜ parameter>, invoke> or
calls> is still cut there: the argument is dropped or truncated and streaming
can end with unterminated JSON. Add a structural lookahead in the TOOL_ARGS
state: a parameter closer ends a value only when whitespace and a new
parameter head, or the end of the call's arguments, follow; an invoke/calls
closer ends a call only once its arguments are closed, and is otherwise held
until the next tokens show whether it was structure (end of stream resolves it
as structure). The provenance rule is kept unchanged and runs first.
Reasoning and content parsing are unchanged. Every closer kept as text is
logged. VLLM_DSV41_STRUCTURAL_DSML=0 restores the previous behaviour; if the
engine hooks it relies on change shape it logs an error and stays off.
Rule after an idea by Hector Isaza (ecohash-co's report); this is an
independent implementation, no code copied.

Quality implications: Tool-call arguments only. Six cases that previously cut
or dropped an argument are now exact (B, C, D, E, E2, J in the matrix).
Documented changes: a value whose parameter closer the model omitted before
</｜DSML｜ invoke> is kept rather than dropped (N, N2); a value ending with a
literal parameter closer is kept whole (R). A value that contains a parameter
closer followed by whitespace and a parameter head is still read as two
arguments; nothing can tell that apart from real structure. All other cases
match the previous parser byte for byte, streamed and non-streamed.

Tests: 25-case matrix x (non-streaming, four chunkings, two reasoning modes)
against the real DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 tokenizer, run inside the
candidate-60 image (CPU only): stream equals non-stream, streamed JSON always
valid, kill switch byte-identical to the previous parser, and the previous
parser fails the six target cases (instrument check). ALL GATES PASS. Live:
served on a 4x GB10 TP4 lane with the candidate-60 image; tool-call probe
(plain and DSML-quoting arguments, streamed and not) passes.

Upstream status: local patch proposal.
